It's a bug, definitely. In the mean time, use c89, which is the DEC C
compiler (the license is bundled with the OS, so you get it for free).
Full ANSI C and will handle your program nicely:

	% cat bug.c
	typedef enum {a;b} c;
	#include <unistd.h>

	% c89 bug.c
        bug.c:1: error: Missing "}".
        Compilation terminated with errors.

Most of the time the MIPS compilers *do* work though...



