> doesn't already do so) a possible remedy to this problem?

  Congratulations! Your drive has developed the "posessed by evil spirits"
problem.

  This is Fault 09, Lost servo samples. It is caused by any number of things,
including (from most likely to least likely):

  o Bad head
  o Bad read/write preamp module
  o Bad servo module
  o Bad microprocessor module
  o Bad spindle bearing

  Note this *isn't* the list in the service manual - this is the list as up-
dated by Field Service Tech Tips.

  If you have a relatively recent (CS rev K or higher, I *think) microprocessor
module, you can determine the head number that is failing. If it's always the
same head, it will be either the head or preamp module.

  Open the drive (remove 4 screws on rear top cover, remove plastic cover, open
pack cover, unscrew metal shroud on rear top cover exposing DB-25 connector on
board with green handles). Stick a terminal in there set to 300 baud and let
the drive run until it faults. Then mail me with what the terminal says.

