Your contributions are appreciated.

The essence of the replies I have received is that the Wren, MAXTOR, HP, and
Fujitsu drives are known to be compatible with the DECStation, and there are
also several vendors now offering true equivalents to DEC's RZs.  No one
suggested that I stay from a particular vendor.  You probably won't go wrong
if you choose a Wren, MAXTOR, Fujitsu, HP, or RZ-equivalent from any reputable
vendor -- the ability of the vendor to support the product is likely to be a
major factor in your decision.  Ask about warranties, support, service, etc.
before you make a committment.

And don't forget DEC.  They do sell disks that work with DECStations, and
although their prices tend to be higher than the third-party vendors, there
may be something to be said for being sure of having no compatibility
problems, for one-stop shopping, for DEC's warranty and service, etc.

There are many vendors out there.  If you can locate a recent copy of
_Digital_Review_ or _Digital_News_, you will find a number of advertisements
near the back.  Following are the vendors I am aware of; there may be others.
