Here's what I am trying to say:

On the server side, you need to tell the server what transports it will
accept.  This is done in sys$manager:decw$private_server_setup.com.  If
you don't have that file on your system, then it has a template file
(sys$manager:decw$private_server_setup.template) which you can use.
There is a line in there:

decw$server_transports == "x,y,z"

Where x, y, and z are transport names.  You can have any number, but
they must be in there for the server to accept them.

On the client side, you can find out what transports are available
simply by doing the following command:

$ dir sys$share:decw$transport_*.exe

You'll see all your favorite transports listed.  For the "set display",
you only put whatever the "*" is replaced with (i.e. decnet, local,
tcpip, etc.).  Even if they show up in the directory, the server has to
expect them as shown above.  Otherwise, they won't work.

