In article <1992Jan18.121011.16107@pronto.mh.nl>, jv@mh.nl (Johan Vromans) writes:
|> I know it is possible to run a VAXstation w/o its graphics hardware.
|> Can someone tell me how to obtain this? Not how to remove the
|> hardware, but how to configure the station that it boots w/o it?
|> 
|> Thanks for sharing!
|> 	Johan

In the file /etc/ttys, change the off in the console line to an on...
(Like so...)

console "/etc/getty std.9600" vt100     on      secure  # console terminal

and add a # to the beginning of the last line (which looks like this)

#:0 "/usr/bin/login -P /usr/bin/Xprompter  (more stuff here but too long)

Then type the command "kill -1 1"

Of course, you have to be root...

