>Having little experiance with X terminals, am I missing any other important
>issues?

We have NCD19b, VT1200 and one VXT 2000.  The missing item in your
list for comparison is performance, i.e. Xstones rating.  My list
shows the following:

NCD19b		17,000 Xstones
NCD19		32,000 Xstones
VT1200		10,000 Xstones
VXT2000		72,000 Xstones

The VXT2000 is a screamer.  I really like it and I have had all 3 on
my desk at one time or another.  It comes with support for running X
over LAT which is a nice feature.  It also supports TCP/IP, Telnet,
etc.

The other thing I like about it is it comes in 2 flavors, stand-alone
as the VT1200 is, and server-based which is what we're using.  Our
Infoserver loads the terminal. It works very nicely and doesn't burden
the VAX with this.

Nice terminal. I recommend it.









