Another guess: your /etc/ttys may not be correct. Look for the (usually)
last line where the dxsession is launched. An error in there will cause
the condition you are stating (prompter starting and dying and starting
and ....).
This is mine for a DECstation 3100 under Ultrix 4.2

:0 "/usr/bin/login -P /usr/bin/Xprompter -C /usr/bin/dxsession -e" none on secu
re window="/usr/bin/Xws bc fp+ /usr/local/lib/X11/fonts/misc/"
