Organization: Box Hill Systems Corporation, NYC
Date: Tue, 21 Jan 1992 22:41:18 GMT

My original query:

>Has anyone been successful using a Sun (Sony) or HP CD-ROM drive on their
>DECstation?  I'm about to get a 5000/240, and need to know if I can use one of
>these drives to boot and install Ultrix.

It seems that the answer is "maybe".  I found out that DEC machines expect
CD-ROM drives to conform to the Phillips/Sony CD-ROM standard, so the Sony
drive used by Sun should work (one respondent verified that they knew of
someone who used a Sun drive on a DEC machine, and Sun said "yes, our Sony
drives adhere to that standard").  However, one person warned me that DEC used
special firmware like Sun, so it might not work (I'm hoping that special
firmware simply implements the Phillips/Sony standard and not some useless
proprietary mumbo-jumbo: after all, who do they think they are, IBM? :-) ).

There has been no indication that an HP drive would work.  I'm going to try my
luck and order Ultrix on CD-ROM and hope I can use my Sun drive to load it.

