I had the same problem a couple of month ago.  Look into the drive manual,
the jumpers on the drive are probably set to SCSI level 2 and Synchronous 
modde transfer. Change them so it's SCSI-1 and disbale synchronous mode 
transfer.  It should then work fine.  

I suggest you call whoever sold you the drives first.  My drives were
Fujitsu M2261S (350 MB model), but they had the same behavior: the first
command send to the drive after a reboot would fail.  Using rzdisk to query
the drive after a reboot would return some "mode sense" error.


