We have a VAXstation 3200 (VMS 5.4-2) with an MDB-DR11W (Rev C) board that
works fine for a 33-bit color display system (I2S IVAS).  The software uses a
specially written GADRIVER instead of the standard XADRIVER issued by DEC.  We
have so far unsuccessfully tried to use the XADRIVER to hook up different
display device (developed in house) using the same MDB-DR11W board.  The manual
that came with the board says you must patch the XADRIVER to fool the system
into thinking the board is a DR11W (UNIBUS version) instead of a DR11WA (QBUS
version), which we did.  The problem we are having is that QIOW read calls only
half work.  The status return block shows normal successful completion and the
corrent number of bytes actually read but there is no data actually written to
the user's buffer in the program.  I made sure by presetting the buffer with
different values before issuing the QIOW.  We also made sure data is
transferred between the user device and controller by hanging a logic analyzer
on the data lines. The handshaking logic appears to work. We are still trying
other ideas but I just like to know if anyone else knows about any problems
with the MDB-DR11W board and the XADRIVER under VMS 5.4-2.  Any clues are also
welcomed.  Thanks.

