We run VS2000's with a stripped-down Ultrix 3.1 and MIT X11R4 on a 40Mb
disk.  Not much room left, but it does boot and allow you an xterm and
window manager.  We get the frills over NFS.  You can't get RIS to
install Ultrix on such a small disk; you have to copy the root and the
bits of /usr you want from a bigger machine, e.g.

    # mkfs or newfs the a partition
    # mount the partition on /mnt
    # cd /mnt
    # rsh somehost -n dump 0f - / | /etc/restore rf -
    edit rc.local to conform to the new host
    
    Repeat for /usr, except you may not want all of it so tar may be
    a better dump/restore method.
