> From article <1991Oct22.174103.22886@sbcs.sunysb.edu>, by sbarrkum@libserv1.ic.sunysb.edu (Se kumarakulasinghe):
>> 
> I've had an LNO3 connected up to my XT clone before.  I was just using
> its serial port at 9600.  The XT was set up to do something like
>   mode com1:9600,n,8,1
>   mode lpt1:=com1:
> or something to redirect lpt1 to the com1 port.  Check your manuals for
> the exact syntax of the mode command.  I only used it for text printing, 
> and as I remember, I would get a "6" error on the printer when I printed, 
> and would take it offline and back online again and it would print ok.
> Drivers?  Who knows?

	The "6" error indicates communications are in progress.  If it
	continues to flash after the print comes out it usually indicates
	your handshaking is not working properly.  The LN03 has its
	handshaking implemented via pin 11 !!! on its RS-232 interface.
	Cross pin 11 over to the relevant pin on the PC end and most of
	your problems will be over.

	If you try and use the portrait fonts in landscape or vice versa,
	the LN03 will try to rotate them for you.  Unfortunately, this
	takes a little time and if you don't have at least one additional
	memory cartridge (proprietry DEC, expensive for what it is) then
	to avoid memory problems you need to clear the font memory each
	time you invoke a rotated font - I fiddled for a long while trying
	to make that work satisfactorily, we bought the memory in the end.


