I'm now preparing to upgrade the last of our systems--the file
server system, and I have one question about the /etc/exports
file.  Under 4.1, I could give root access to a couple special
machines but user-level access only to the rest of the clients
by specifying multiple occurrences of the same exported file system
in /etc/exports.  Example:

	/usr	-r=0 foo1
	/usr	foo2 foo3

foo1 has root access but foo2 and foo3 have user-level access only
(this works, despite the fact that the man page states the contrary).
Under 4.2 however, I cannot specify an exported file system multiple
times in the exports file; thus I now specify user-level access with:

	/usr	foo2 foo3 foo4
