This is the second RFD for the creation of an unmoderated group,
comp.unix.bsd.

The proposed group would act as a forum for discussion about BSD Unix
and its derivatives.  BSD Unix and its derivatives run on a wide range
of platforms, ranging from PDP11s (2.11) to PC/RTs (AOS 4.3).  The large
range of installed sites, and the reported impending releases of various
commercial and non-commercial BSD-derivatives seems to indicate the need
for such a group.

Dick Dunn <rcd@raven.eklektix.com> neatly summarised the likely use of
such a group: 1) discussion about BSD 4.3, being replaced by 2) discussion
about converting to BSD 4.4, and ultimately becoming 3) discussion about
the new BSD 4.4. If traffic becomes too heavy, subsidiary newsgroups may
be formed for various versions.

If no major disagreement occurs, a Call For Vote will be issued on
January 12, 1992.  Detailed information on the voting procedure will be
included in that posting.

