In <1992Jan4.005243.14819@fallst.UUCP> tkevans@fallst.UUCP (Tim Evans) writes:

| We have a VAX 11/750, running 4.2BSD, on which 'df'
| insists the root file system is 99 percent full, not matter
| what we remove.  Can anyone point me in the right direction?
| (Aside from junking the antique, that is.)

one of the files you removed was probably still open and being
written to.  If whatever is writing is running wild, every time
you remove another file to make more space, the unlinked file
(which still occupies disk space as long as it is in use) will
grow to use it up.

Kill any 'unusual' programs, or worst case, go to single user
mode or reboot.
--

     Dave Olson (olson@sgi.com)


