   you remove another file to make more space, the unlinked file
   (which still occupies disk space as long as it is in use) will
   grow to use it up.

Another possibility is that there are files hidden behind a mount
point like /usr (say). These files will will only become visible when
no filesystem are mounted at the mount points (i.e. when the system
comes up in single user mode with only the / filesystem active).

		Jim


